<Base title="About" description="About TC Lee — hardware BD, civil defense organizer, builder.">
  <div class="prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I started a company, shut it down, went back into a corporate job — and didn't leave the startup mindset behind.
      That's the short version.
    </p>

    <p>
      The longer version: I'm TC Lee, based in Taipei. My work crosses three areas that don't usually overlap —
      industrial hardware, community resilience, and AI implementation. I write about all three.
    </p>

    <h2>Hardware BD in Europe</h2>
    <p>
      I do business development for <a href="https://axiomtek.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Axiomtek</a>
      in European transportation and retail markets. Specifically: the embedded computers inside railway carriages,
      fleet vehicles, transit kiosks, and roadside infrastructure. It's a niche world where
      certification (EN50155, E-Mark, IP65) matters more than benchmark scores, and where
      a 10-year product lifecycle is the norm. I attend InnoTrans, follow EU rail tenders,
      and work with equipment makers across Scandinavia and Western Europe.
    </p>

    <h2>Civil defense</h2>
    <p>
      I co-founded <strong>港湖民防團</strong> (Ganghu Civil Defense Team), a volunteer organization
      in Taipei's Neihu/Ganghu district. We run training in emergency medical response (I'm EMT certified),
      amateur radio communications, and community preparedness. We hold weekly sessions and quarterly field exercises.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm also doing structured research on civil defense behavior — specifically, what moves people from
      awareness to action. I've joined Ukraine × Taiwan hybrid warfare workshops and follow civil defense
      developments internationally. This is serious work to me, not a side interest.
    </p>

    <h2>AI from inside</h2>
    <p>
      Since returning to corporate, I've been pushing AI adoption from the inside — leading implementation POCs
      at Axiomtek, building AI-assisted workflows for BD and operations, and thinking about where LLMs
      actually create durable value versus where they're noise.
    </p>
    <p>
      The interesting position I find myself in: I'm simultaneously a user of these tools and someone
      building the infrastructure to use them at scale. That dual perspective shapes most of what I write.
    </p>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>
      Self-taught iOS developer and Shopify builder. Started and ran a company. Now in hardware B2B with a
      software lens. I've written technical articles in Chinese on
      <a href="https://tc-lee.medium.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Medium</a> since 2023, and
      practitioner pieces in English on
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/t-c-lee" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a> since 2026.
      This site is the permanent home for writing I want to last.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Best reached on <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/t-c-lee" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
